From 0ae50ef681dfc581a94cd90bf9f36431c7acb7f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuppusamy R <kuppusamy433@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:52:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix static channel PDU reassembly for multi-chunk messages

channel_client_post_message() sized the reassembly stream to the first
chunk's dataLength instead of the whole PDU's totalLength. When a static
virtual channel PDU spans more than one CHANNEL_CHUNK_LENGTH (1600 byte)
chunk, Stream_EnsureRemainingCapacity() later rounds the capacity up to
the next 128-byte boundary, so on the final chunk
Stream_Capacity(data_in) != Stream_GetPosition(data_in) and the PDU is
rejected with 'read error' / ERROR_INTERNAL_ERROR (1359), tearing down
the session. This broke e.g. Remmina clipboard paste of ~750+ characters
(cliprdr FormatDataResponse split across chunks), regression from
ead997147.

Allocate the reassembly stream to totalLength on CHANNEL_FLAG_FIRST.

Fixes #13486

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 channels/client/addin.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/channels/client/addin.c b/channels/client/addin.c
index 9b3d040..90ce1ac 100644
--- a/channels/client/addin.c
+++ b/channels/client/addin.c
@@ -664,11 +664,11 @@ UINT channel_client_post_message(void* MsgsHandle, LPVOID pData, UINT32 dataLeng
 
 		if (internals->data_in)
 		{
-			if (!Stream_EnsureCapacity(internals->data_in, dataLength))
+			if (!Stream_EnsureCapacity(internals->data_in, totalLength))
 				return CHANNEL_RC_NO_MEMORY;
 		}
 		else
-			internals->data_in = Stream_New(nullptr, dataLength);
+			internals->data_in = Stream_New(nullptr, totalLength);
 	}
 
 	if (!(data_in = internals->data_in))
-- 
